# Configurable keybindings

When adding or changing keybindings in lnav-rs:

- Wire them through `[keys]`, `[details_keys]`, and/or `[sidebar_keys]` (see `src/keys.rs` defaults), not hardcoded intercepts in input handlers.
- Hardcode only rare exceptions that already exist for structural reasons (e.g. `:` / `q` leaving overlay/sidebar focus for command-mode/quit) — do not add new hardcoded action keys. Esc closing panes should stay a `[keys]` binding (`view current off`).
- Prefer context via `[details_keys]` / `[sidebar_keys]` overlays when panes need different bindings for the same key.
- Document new bindings in the README key tables and example `[keys]` / `[details_keys]` / `[sidebar_keys]` snippets.
